          <text x="35" y="16" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#e0e7ff">Room O2 Monitor:</text>
          <text x="140" y="16" font-size="10" font-mono" font-weight="bold" fill="#4ade80" id="svg-o2-val">20.9%</text>
          <text x="35" y="28" font-size="8" font-mono" fill="#a5b4fc">OSHA 1910.146 Safe Level</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Scientific Foundations Section -->
  <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 mb-10">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">{d.scienceTitle}</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">{d.scienceSub}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
      <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-400"></span>
          1. Supercritical Nitrogen Phase State &amp; Eutectic Vitrification
        </h3>
        <p>
          At pressures exceeding its thermodynamic critical point (<span class="font-mono text-cyan-400">P_c = 34.00 bar</span>, <span class="font-mono text-cyan-400">T_c = -146.95 °C</span>), liquid nitrogen transitions into a dense fluid phase characterized by liquid-like density (<span class="font-mono">&rho; &approx; 808 kg/m³</span>) and gas-like viscosity and diffusivity. When introduced into biological food matrices, dense supercritical nitrogen rapidly infiltrates cellular micropores without creating liquid meniscus tension.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the operating temperature is maintained strictly below the matrix eutectic point (<span class="font-mono">T &le; -35.0 °C</span>), intracellular water is instantaneously immobilized into amorphous vitrified ice. Unlike slow conventional blast freezing (cooling rates &lt; 0.5 °C/min) that breeds destructive hexagonal ice crystals (&gt; 50 &mu;m) that rupture bacterial cell walls, SND-BP achieves ultra-fast cryogenic vitrification (&gt; 120 °C/min), preserving over 98% viability of fragile probiotic strains like <em>Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG</em> and <em>Bifidobacterium lactis</em>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
          2. Supersonic Shock Depressurization &amp; Flash Sublimation
        </h3>
        <p>
          The saturated cryogenic matrix is continuously discharged across a converging-diverging (De Laval) supersonic expansion nozzle into a subatmospheric chamber (<span class="font-mono">P_exp &le; 0.50 mbar</span>). As the fluid depressurizes from 45 bar to sub-millibar levels in under 3 milliseconds, the dissolved nitrogen gas undergoes violent volumetric phase expansion (<span class="font-mono">&Delta;V / V_0 &gt; 650</span>).
        </p>
        <p>
          The explosive nucleation of expanding nitrogen micro-bubbles mechanically forces open an interconnected honeycomb matrix. Simultaneously, Joule-Thomson cooling combines with the immense vacuum vapor pressure gradient across the water triple point (<span class="font-mono">6.11 mbar, 0.01 °C</span>) to drive instant flash sublimation of surface and boundary-layer water molecules, stripping over 96% of initial moisture in seconds rather than 24 hours required by batch freeze dryers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400"></span>
          3. Micro-Cellular Aeration &amp; Weibull Crispness Fracture
        </h3>
        <p>
          Texture and shelf-life are governed by final water activity (<span class="font-mono">a_w &le; 0.20</span>) and glass-transition temperature (<span class="font-mono">T_g &gt; 25 °C</span>). The microscopic cellular structure produced by SND-BP features uniform pore diameters between 15 and 45 &mu;m with cell wall thicknesses below 2.5 &mu;m.
        </p>
        <p>
          Under mechanical puncture testing (TA.XT Plus Texture Analyzer), the brittle matrix exhibits multi-peak acoustic micro-fracture profiles with peak fracture forces between 11.0 and 16.5 N. When evaluated via Weibull failure distribution, the product demonstrates an exceptionally high fracture event density (> 45 fracture peaks/mm), conferring the signature airy, melt-in-mouth crispness prized in premium functional snack crisps and instant dissolvable coffee extract beads.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400"></span>
          4. ASME Section VIII &amp; OSHA 1910.146 Cryogenic Safety
        </h3>
        <p>
          Operating at 40–60 bar cryogenic temperatures introduces severe mechanical and environmental hazards: low-temperature metal embrittlement, cryogenic thermal expansion pressure traps, and asphyxiation from nitrogen vapor expansion (1 liter of liquid nitrogen expands into 694 liters of gas at ambient conditions).
        </p>
        <p>
          The skid is fabricated from ASME SA-240 Type 316L stainless steel certified with Charpy V-notch impact testing at -196 °C (<span class="font-mono">KV &ge; 80 J</span>). Every isolated piping run is safeguarded by dual ASME UV-stamped cryogenic thermal relief valves set to 110% design pressure. Surrounding room atmospheres are continuously interlocked with redundant galvanic O2 sensors (<span class="font-mono">OSHA 29 CFR § 1910.146</span>, auto-vent alarms triggered at O2 &lt; 19.5%), ensuring uncompromising worker and plant safety.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Engineering Data Reference Table -->
  <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-8">
    <div class="mb-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-1">{d.tableTitle}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-xs text-left border border-hairline rounded-xl overflow-hidden font-mono">
